"Even better if the
girls are up for it too"

1489
01:37:49.364 --> 01:37:52.950
"And some chicken with
it only makes things better!"

1490
01:37:56.496 --> 01:38:00.041
"Even better if the
girls are up for it too"

1491
01:38:37.161 --> 01:38:38.996
Why is that chubby
uncle so angry?

1492
01:38:42.166 --> 01:38:43.292
He must be hungry.

1493
01:38:50.383 --> 01:38:52.844
Everyone's really serious!
Something's up. Let's find out.

1494
01:39:01.727 --> 01:39:02.728
Mom!

1495
01:39:09.735 --> 01:39:10.862
What's happening?

1496
01:39:11.070 --> 01:39:12.071
It's too small.

1497
01:39:12.405 --> 01:39:13.613
Duke's tunic?

1498
01:39:13.614 --> 01:39:15.032
It's not funny!

1499
01:39:15.241 --> 01:39:17.910
The car Rajji gave
Duke is too small.

1500
01:39:18.286 --> 01:39:20.288
Oh! And their family
won't fit in it.

1501
01:39:20.913 --> 01:39:23.790
No! They saw the key
and thought it was a big car!

1502
01:39:23.791 --> 01:39:25.585
Oh! They were confused
by the big key!

1503
01:39:25.835 --> 01:39:28.004
I don't believe this!
Now?

1504
01:39:28.796 --> 01:39:31.340
They want a big
car or no wedding.

1505
01:39:31.549 --> 01:39:33.259
But Aunty, a gift is a gift.

1506
01:39:33.759 --> 01:39:37.847
Not gift... Dowry.
Anyway, what's the solution?

1507
01:39:38.473 --> 01:39:40.224
Well, Rajji doesn't
have the money.

1508
01:39:40.641 --> 01:39:45.855
So, we've decided to give them
ourjewelry as a guarantee.

1509
01:39:46.397 --> 01:39:47.899
You wait, I'll be back.

1510
01:39:50.735 --> 01:39:51.736
Dowry.

1511
01:39:52.695 --> 01:39:53.905
Really?

1512
01:40:01.454 --> 01:40:02.788
Ananya...

1513
01:40:03.789 --> 01:40:04.832
Ananya!

1514
01:40:05.374 --> 01:40:06.626
Excuse me?

1515
01:40:09.795 --> 01:40:12.757
May I say something?

1516
01:40:13.424 --> 01:40:14.509
What?

1517
01:40:15.426 --> 01:40:18.846
Before you give away your
jewelry, can I talk to Duke?

1518
01:40:19.305 --> 01:40:21.474
No, no. You don't
get involved in this.

1519
01:40:22.141 --> 01:40:23.809
Please, let me try.

1520
01:40:24.644 --> 01:40:26.395
I promise there'll
be no problem.

1521
01:40:45.540 --> 01:40:46.541
Duke...

1522
01:40:47.583 --> 01:40:48.667
Hi.

1523
01:40:48.668 --> 01:40:49.669
Hi!

1524
01:40:49.961 --> 01:40:51.337
What's your salary?

1525
01:40:52.213 --> 01:40:53.172
What?!

1526
01:40:54.215 --> 01:40:57.051
- How much do you earn per month?
- What?!

1527
01:41:10.773 --> 01:41:12.691
25 thousand.
Who are you?

1528
01:41:12.692 --> 01:41:13.776
Doesn't matter.

1529
01:41:14.235 --> 01:41:15.944
I earn 50.

1530
01:41:15.945 --> 01:41:21.242
Can you tell me why you
deserve such grand wedding?

1531
01:41:22.243 --> 01:41:24.036
And you're getting
a car for dowry!

1532
01:41:25.288 --> 01:41:26.539
I'm the boy!

1533
01:41:26.998 --> 01:41:28.958
Really? SO?

1534
01:41:30.459 --> 01:41:31.627
$0!

1535
01:41:32.587 --> 01:41:33.671
So...

1536
01:41:35.214 --> 01:41:36.507
Look at Minty carefully.

1537
01:41:38.217 --> 01:41:42.346
You think you had a shot with
her without an arranged marriage?

1538
01:41:42.722 --> 01:41:45.349
- This is the limit!
- Oh no, I'm not done.

1539
01:41:50.646 --> 01:41:52.815
Do you know what they've
been through for this wedding?

1540
01:41:54.066 --> 01:41:55.234
They're in debt.

1541
01:41:55.651 --> 01:41:57.153
And this car?

1542
01:41:57.528 --> 01:41:59.947
It costs as much as 15
years of your holiday bonuses!

1543
01:42:00.531 --> 01:42:03.618
And the car you want, you won't be
able to afford even after retirement.

1544
01:42:04.702 --> 01:42:07.163
If you twist their arm,
they'll give you the bigger car...

1545
01:42:07.496 --> 01:42:09.749
but don't you
have any self-respect?!

1546
01:42:18.299 --> 01:42:20.259
Look, you can get the big car.

1547
01:42:21.302 --> 01:42:25.139
Now you decide; do you want
to get married honourably...

1548
01:42:25.598 --> 01:42:29.518
or let go of a girl
like Minty because of a car?

1549
01:42:31.354 --> 01:42:33.147
Ananya... let it go.

1550
01:42:33.981 --> 01:42:35.650
Two minutes, Uncle.

1551
01:42:37.360 --> 01:42:39.153
You have two
minutes to decide.

1552
01:42:41.739 --> 01:42:43.949
- I want to go to my Mummy.
- Why?

1553
01:42:44.492 --> 01:42:46.369
Why are you so dominating?!

1554
01:42:46.619 --> 01:42:48.329
Please, let me to go
to my Mummy.

1555
01:42:48.871 --> 01:42:50.956
Okay. We'll all go.

1556
01:42:51.874 --> 01:42:53.125
Come on then!

1557
01:42:58.381 --> 01:43:00.257
Mummy! I like this car.

1558
01:43:00.508 --> 01:43:02.592
But, the deal was for big car!

1559
01:43:02.593 --> 01:43:05.012
Can't I buy a
big car on my own?

1560
01:43:05.346 --> 01:43:08.724
Don't I have any self-respect?
Stop this silly fighting.

1561
01:43:09.016 --> 01:43:10.142
What's the decision?

1562
01:43:11.018 --> 01:43:14.814
Sorry, madam. Done.
Okay? I want to get married!

1563
01:43:19.193 --> 01:43:20.944
So Duke's parents
relented and...

1564
01:43:20.945 --> 01:43:23.531
Ananya became a
hero to my family.

1565
01:43:28.828 --> 01:43:29.829
Thank you.

1566
01:43:30.287 --> 01:43:31.247
Here.

1567
01:43:32.581 --> 01:43:34.542
Rajji and Shipra loved her.

1568
01:43:35.960 --> 01:43:37.044
SO... yes?

1569
01:43:37.461 --> 01:43:38.421
Yes...

1570
01:43:38.754 --> 01:43:41.006
- But what about her folks?
- They've agreed.

1571
01:43:44.385 --> 01:43:45.469
Look, Ananya.

1572
01:43:45.845 --> 01:43:48.681
Both families need to
have an understanding.

1573
01:43:52.143 --> 01:43:53.769
You remember the convocation?

1574
01:43:59.859 --> 01:44:01.068
Your mom's right.

1575
01:44:01.777 --> 01:44:02.778
Meaning?

1576
01:44:03.320 --> 01:44:07.700
I mean our parents have agreed,
but they still don't like each other.

1577
01:44:08.033 --> 01:44:10.911
So what? It's not like
they're getting married.

1578
01:44:11.662 --> 01:44:14.957
If we've decided to make
them happy, let's do it right?

1579
01:44:16.751 --> 01:44:18.794
They have to meet again.

1580
01:44:19.420 --> 01:44:22.214
No, now enough, okay?
I can't play this game forever.

1581
01:44:22.631 --> 01:44:25.384
What more can I do?
Get Mom to Chennai?

1582
01:44:25.676 --> 01:44:26.719
No!

1583
01:44:28.262 --> 01:44:29.472
Let's go on vacation?

1584
01:44:29.889 --> 01:44:30.931
All of us!

1585
01:44:31.265 --> 01:44:33.684
That way they'll
get to know each other.

1586
01:44:34.852 --> 01:44:35.936
Please?

1587
01:44:37.438 --> 01:44:39.940
In this world, what's the most
important reason to get married?

1588
01:44:40.608 --> 01:44:41.567
Love!

1589
01:44:42.777 --> 01:44:45.696
In India, however,
there are a few more steps...

1590
01:44:46.280 --> 01:44:48.698
The girl's family
has to love the boy.

1591
01:44:48.699 --> 01:44:50.326
The boy's family
has to love the girl.

1592
01:44:51.202 --> 01:44:53.077
The boy's family has
to love the girl's family...

1593
01:44:53.078 --> 01:44:55.289
and the girl's family
has to love the boy's family.

1594
01:44:56.207 --> 01:44:57.458
After all this...

1595
01:44:57.750 --> 01:45:01.754
if the boy and girl still love
each other, then they get married.

1596
01:45:14.767 --> 01:45:18.728
What's bugging them? Look how
they're standing there looking surly.

1597
01:45:18.729 --> 01:45:19.979
Nothing like that!

1598
01:45:19.980 --> 01:45:21.774
What do you know of
the politics of marriage?

1599
01:45:22.691 --> 01:45:23.942
Thank you.

1600
01:45:23.943 --> 01:45:26.821
By the way, Krish... This
hotel must be very expensive.

1601
01:45:27.571 --> 01:45:32.201
Yes, but I've promised to hold
the next YES Bank conference here.

1602
01:45:32.910 --> 01:45:34.370
So, they've given
me a discount.

1603
01:45:35.037 --> 01:45:37.957
Come now, smile, please?
Smile.

1604
01:45:39.792 --> 01:45:41.084
Namaste, Kavita.

1605
01:45:41.085 --> 01:45:42.794
- Namaste.
- Hello, Aunty.

1606
01:45:42.795 --> 01:45:43.921
Hello.

1607
01:45:45.923 --> 01:45:49.092
Oh! This is for you.
Silk sari.

1608
01:45:49.093 --> 01:45:50.301
Tussar silk.

1609
01:45:50.302 --> 01:45:52.680
Specially for you
from Assam Emporium.

1610
01:45:53.347 --> 01:45:54.473
Thank you.

1611
01:45:54.723 --> 01:45:57.058
Our silk saris
are also very famous.

1612
01:45:57.059 --> 01:45:59.061
- Of course!
- Kanjeevaram saris.

1613
01:46:03.190 --> 01:46:05.067
Your husband couldn't come?

1614
01:46:06.318 --> 01:46:09.404
He's not keeping well.

1615
01:46:09.405 --> 01:46:12.741
The doctors have asked
him not to travel by air.

1616
01:46:13.576 --> 01:46:15.077
Isn't there a
train from Delhi?

1617
01:46:16.453 --> 01:46:17.913
We don't travel by train.

1618
01:46:18.205 --> 01:46:21.332
Their toilets
are awfully small.

1619
01:46:21.333 --> 01:46:22.918
Shall we go, mom?

1620
01:46:23.878 --> 01:46:27.088
You know we Punjabis
are really large-hearted.

1621
01:46:27.089 --> 01:46:30.133
We never greet our
in-laws empty handed.

1622
01:46:30.134 --> 01:46:32.468
Especially, the boy's mother!

1623
01:46:32.469 --> 01:46:35.722
It's considered bad luck...

1624
01:46:35.723 --> 01:46:38.851
Shall we go sightseeing tomorrow?
Coffee Shop at 11 am?

1625
01:46:39.852 --> 01:46:42.396
Sightseeing! With her?

1626
01:46:42.813 --> 01:46:44.647
- Mom.
- No.

1627
01:46:44.648 --> 01:46:45.858
Dad, please!

1628
01:46:46.275 --> 01:46:48.068
Done! Sightseeing!

1629
01:46:49.403 --> 01:46:53.114
Oh, the hotel has upgraded us.

1630
01:46:53.115 --> 01:46:54.782
Please, take the bigger room.

1631
01:46:54.783 --> 01:46:56.160
There are more of you.

1632
01:46:56.660 --> 01:46:57.828
What about us!

1633
01:47:02.708 --> 01:47:04.001
- Let's go.
- No, no Aunty!

1634
01:47:09.131 --> 01:47:10.465
How shameless!

1635
01:47:10.466 --> 01:47:12.050
Who?! Him?

1636
01:47:12.051 --> 01:47:13.260
No. Them.

1637
01:47:13.719 --> 01:47:15.845
Who makes the groom
pick up luggage?!

1638
01:47:15.846 --> 01:47:18.222
- I'm not the "groom".
- What then, the bride?!

1639
01:47:18.223 --> 01:47:20.184
Don't talk rubbish!

1640
01:47:20.726 --> 01:47:22.894
What was the need to
give them the big room?

1641
01:47:22.895 --> 01:47:24.229
There's more of them?

1642
01:47:24.688 --> 01:47:25.897
Sure, sure.

1643
01:47:25.898 --> 01:47:29.568
Those poor guys mustn't have
ever seen such a grand hotel.

1644
01:47:30.611 --> 01:47:32.570
You know what their
biggest mistake was?

1645
01:47:32.571 --> 01:47:34.907
They met the boy's
mother empty-handed!

1646
01:47:35.407 --> 01:47:40.245
And that Madrasan called
ME uncultured at that conversation.

1647
01:47:41.080 --> 01:47:44.708
Why did I have to get carried
away and buy her a silk sari?

1648
01:47:46.168 --> 01:47:48.170
Rs. 2,000 down the drain.

1649
01:47:55.010 --> 01:47:56.679
How pretty the sea is!

1650
01:47:57.888 --> 01:48:01.266
Yes, but Chennai's sea is
cleaner and prettier than this!

1651
01:48:16.156 --> 01:48:18.909
Hanging Gardens!
What a nice view!

1652
01:48:19.618 --> 01:48:22.746
What?!
People are hanged here?!

1653
01:48:24.498 --> 01:48:27.584
It's called Hanging Gardens
because it's on a hill!

1654
01:48:27.960 --> 01:48:31.088
Oh... you scared me...

1655
01:48:42.766 --> 01:48:44.226
Your mom is so rude!

1656
01:48:44.810 --> 01:48:47.980
Your family's not
exactly friendly, either.

1657
01:48:48.689 --> 01:48:49.982
What do we do?

1658
01:48:50.983 --> 01:48:52.401
I have an idea.
But you can't feel bad.

1659
01:48:53.318 --> 01:48:54.403
Depends.

1660
01:48:54.737 --> 01:48:58.907
First, you'll need to get my
mother a really nice present.

1661
01:48:59.616 --> 01:49:01.201
- Okay...
- Next.

1662
01:49:01.577 --> 01:49:04.371
Whenever we're eating out,
insist on paying.

1663
01:49:04.872 --> 01:49:09.043
Snatch her purse if you have to!
Punjabis consider this affection.

1664
01:49:09.376 --> 01:49:10.501
And?

1665
01:49:10.502 --> 01:49:14.547
Third, right now, in the middle
of this beach, you and I should...

1666
01:49:14.548 --> 01:49:17.468
Absolutely not! Not until the
wedding. I'm very stressed!

1667
01:49:17.760 --> 01:49:19.135
But it's a great
stress buster!

1668
01:49:19.136 --> 01:49:20.429
Control yourself, Krish!

1669
01:49:23.182 --> 01:49:25.642
You know what the worst
part of getting married is?

1670
01:49:26.060 --> 01:49:28.896
First, you have to discuss
clothes and jewelry.

1671
01:49:29.813 --> 01:49:33.317
Second, all women lose their
tempers at the same time! I mean...

1672
01:49:36.278 --> 01:49:37.946
So many demands already...

1673
01:49:38.489 --> 01:49:40.157
God knows what will
happen in the future!

1674
01:49:52.252 --> 01:49:53.419
This is for you.

1675
01:49:53.420 --> 01:49:55.464
Oh, you shouldn't have!

1676
01:49:57.382 --> 01:49:58.467
This too.

1677
01:50:00.010 --> 01:50:01.762
Please come! Sit!

1678
01:50:10.479 --> 01:50:12.897
Have some chicken!
It's delicious!

1679
01:50:12.898 --> 01:50:14.358
We're vegetarians...

1680
01:50:15.400 --> 01:50:16.693
Oh.

1681
01:50:17.402 --> 01:50:19.613
Well... no problem.

1682
01:50:34.503 --> 01:50:35.796
Who would have thought...

1683
01:50:36.046 --> 01:50:37.965
One day the kids would
be introducing their parents!

1684
01:50:39.049 --> 01:50:42.719
It came as a
shock to us, too...

1685
01:50:43.137 --> 01:50:46.389
But once we met Krish,
we were okay.

1686
01:50:46.390 --> 01:50:51.019
Oh, don't pull my leg!
You must have thanked your stars...

1687
01:50:51.270 --> 01:50:54.857
that your daughter found
such a handsome and qualified boy!

1688
01:50:57.109 --> 01:51:00.237
Actually, 90 percent of
Tamilians are highly qualified.

1689
01:51:00.696 --> 01:51:03.657
All of Ananya's uncles
are engineers in the USA.

1690
01:51:03.949 --> 01:51:07.785
I'm sorry but 90% Tamilians
aren't fair-skinned either!

1691
01:51:07.786 --> 01:51:09.413
Mom! Mom, let's have dessert.

1692
01:51:10.289 --> 01:51:11.623
Oh by the way...

1693
01:51:11.874 --> 01:51:15.627
Krish's uncles are also
very rich and successful!

1694
01:51:16.170 --> 01:51:20.257
Ananya met them at our place!
What a magnificent wedding it was!

1695
01:51:21.133 --> 01:51:26.430
My brother gave his son-in-law
a car as a wedding present!

1696
01:51:31.185 --> 01:51:34.605
How lucky you are... to have
landed such a wonderful boy!

1697
01:51:35.022 --> 01:51:36.356
Luck by chance!

1698
01:51:36.773 --> 01:51:38.317
Mom, what are you saying!

1699
01:51:38.817 --> 01:51:41.153
We haven't conned
your son into this.

1700
01:51:41.862 --> 01:51:44.114
He came to our house everyday,
we couldn't say no.

1701
01:51:44.573 --> 01:51:45.949
- Mom...
- It's true!

1702
01:51:46.200 --> 01:51:48.410
We're making a big
effort for you, too.

1703
01:51:49.244 --> 01:51:52.539
Everyone knows Krish's father
is against this marriage.

1704
01:51:52.998 --> 01:51:54.583
We're still here, aren't we?

1705
01:51:55.959 --> 01:51:58.045
Well, you're not
doing me any favours.

1706
01:51:58.337 --> 01:52:02.674
Millionaire Punjabi girls
are lining up for my Krish.

1707
01:52:04.134 --> 01:52:05.509
There's no need to yell.
We are educated people.

1708
01:52:05.510 --> 01:52:07.137
- Oh and we're illiterate?!
- Mom...

1709
01:52:07.387 --> 01:52:10.514
He said we.
All of us are educated!

1710
01:52:10.515 --> 01:52:12.893
Shut up!
You're blind to everything!

1711
01:52:13.685 --> 01:52:15.686
Go... live in Chennai
with your in-laws!

1712
01:52:15.687 --> 01:52:17.272
Krish. This is not right.

1713
01:52:17.564 --> 01:52:19.358
- Let it go, mom.
- You be quiet!

1714
01:52:20.484 --> 01:52:21.944
This won't work out.

1715
01:52:22.319 --> 01:52:25.446
She won't keep our child happy.
Look at the things she says!

1716
01:52:25.447 --> 01:52:26.949
What are they muttering
in their code language?

1717
01:52:27.199 --> 01:52:28.282
How would I know?!

1718
01:52:28.283 --> 01:52:29.993
I thought they'd
have taught you by now!

1719
01:52:30.202 --> 01:52:31.745
This is not okay,
let us get going.

1720
01:52:32.329 --> 01:52:33.830
This is way too much. Come.

1721
01:52:34.373 --> 01:52:36.333
- Dad, please...
- That's it! We're leaving!

1722
01:52:55.185 --> 01:52:56.895
Aunty we did
whatever Krish asked.

1723
01:52:57.688 --> 01:52:59.481
But nothing is enough for you.

1724
01:53:00.482 --> 01:53:04.903
Ananya, we'll talk to them...
It's not like that.

1725
01:53:07.114 --> 01:53:08.240
Thanks for lunch.

1726
01:53:14.871 --> 01:53:16.832
So, you told them to
buy these saris for me.

1727
01:53:17.082 --> 01:53:20.043
Yes. What's the point
of doing all this?!

1728
01:53:20.544 --> 01:53:23.255
Of course.
It's always my fault!

1729
01:53:24.756 --> 01:53:25.924
People are right.

1730
01:53:26.550 --> 01:53:28.509
Falling in love changes
the best of men.

1731
01:53:28.510 --> 01:53:29.511
That's not true!

1732
01:53:53.827 --> 01:53:56.913
Did you see how rude
your dear Ananya was to me?

1733
01:53:57.456 --> 01:54:00.542
I know she's a little brazen,
but you were wrong this time, Mom.

1734
01:54:03.086 --> 01:54:04.921
You're going to
treat me as a servant?

1735
01:54:05.797 --> 01:54:09.051
My life is doomed.

1736
01:54:09.426 --> 01:54:11.595
No one is making
you a servant, mom!

1737
01:54:11.803 --> 01:54:15.265
Daughters-in-law
can't be so rude!

1738
01:54:15.807 --> 01:54:16.932
Just think.

1739
01:54:16.933 --> 01:54:19.686
What if Minty speaks
in this way to Duke's mother?!

1740
01:54:20.854 --> 01:54:23.899
We rule our daughters-in-law
with iron fists!

1741
01:54:26.485 --> 01:54:27.569
<i>OKQY -</i>

1742
01:54:28.653 --> 01:54:30.072
You can do it too.

1743
01:54:31.740 --> 01:54:34.451
How! You always take her side.

1744
01:54:34.868 --> 01:54:35.994
I won't!

1745
01:54:37.162 --> 01:54:40.374
Once we're married,
you show her who's the boss!

1746
01:54:41.249 --> 01:54:45.127
You know how passive
her parents are.

1747
01:54:45.128 --> 01:54:46.380
They can't do anything.

1748
01:54:47.255 --> 01:54:50.300
Please just handle
the situation for now.

1749
01:54:51.593 --> 01:54:52.677
Please?

1750
01:54:54.971 --> 01:54:56.014
Fine.

1751
01:54:59.851 --> 01:55:01.061
Ananya.

1752
01:55:01.937 --> 01:55:04.022
- We were just talking about you-
- I heard.

1753
01:55:16.618 --> 01:55:19.121
I wanted to make one
last attempt to fix things.

1754
01:55:21.164 --> 01:55:22.499
But not anymore.

1755
01:55:23.625 --> 01:55:25.460
Ananya, Ananya!
Just listen to me!

1756
01:55:30.757 --> 01:55:32.008
Ananya, please listen to me!

1757
01:55:32.217 --> 01:55:34.052
I was trying to pacify Mom!

1758
01:55:34.719 --> 01:55:36.888
You're telling me the
same lies you told her!

1759
01:55:38.807 --> 01:55:40.976
The problem's not just
your mother. It's you, too.

1760
01:55:44.354 --> 01:55:45.689
We're done, Krish.

1761
01:55:46.273 --> 01:55:47.940
Are you insane?
For such a minor thing...

1762
01:55:47.941 --> 01:55:51.862
Minor thing?! My parents can't
take any more humiliation!

1763
01:55:52.821 --> 01:55:55.281
- They've done a lot for me!
- I can fix this, Ananya.

1764
01:55:55.282 --> 01:55:57.409
By lying to your mother.
Right?

1765
01:56:00.162 --> 01:56:01.788
How many people
will you lie to?

1766
01:56:02.789 --> 01:56:05.208
All your lies will
destroy us one day!

1767
01:56:05.959 --> 01:56:07.335
Everything will be okay.

1768
01:56:08.253 --> 01:56:09.629
We've made a huge mistake...

1769
01:56:11.381 --> 01:56:15.260
You know, Krish, it's
not about the communities...

1770
01:56:16.428 --> 01:56:20.765
it's about the kind of people
we want to spend our lives with.

1771
01:56:23.810 --> 01:56:25.812
Certain things are
just not in our destiny...

1772
01:56:28.398 --> 01:56:29.566
Like this.

1773
01:56:46.416 --> 01:56:49.377
"Without you... there's
no fire in the sun"

1774
01:56:50.587 --> 01:56:53.507
"No song in the songbird"

1775
01:56:54.549 --> 01:56:58.720
"if the moon reigns
with such abandon"

1776
01:56:59.221 --> 01:57:04.351
"Why is there only
darkness in my grasp?"

1777
01:57:11.399 --> 01:57:14.861
"Without you... there's
no spring in the springtime"

1778
01:57:15.654 --> 01:57:18.865
"No waking in wakeness"

1779
01:57:19.908 --> 01:57:23.954
"Without you, my love,"

1780
01:57:24.329 --> 01:57:29.251
"My heart is
a deserted island"

1781
01:57:32.254 --> 01:57:36.174
"These incomplete stories..."

1782
01:57:37.008 --> 01:57:39.886
"And these
incomplete goodbyes"

1783
01:57:40.887 --> 01:57:44.891
"Will they remain
incomplete..."

1784
01:57:45.392 --> 01:57:48.603
"... forever?"

1785
01:57:49.104 --> 01:57:56.486
"These incomplete stories..."

1786
01:57:57.529 --> 01:58:03.827
"And these
incomplete goodbyes"

1787
01:58:05.620 --> 01:58:10.584
"if the moon reigns
with such abandon"

1788
01:58:10.875 --> 01:58:15.630
"Why is there only
darkness in my grasp?"

1789
01:58:34.107 --> 01:58:35.734
I've made fresh,
hot parathas...

1790
01:58:36.067 --> 01:58:37.277
Please eat?

1791
01:58:45.368 --> 01:58:47.287
So... you've stopped talking
to your mother as well?

1792
01:58:48.997 --> 01:58:51.541
What wrong could
she have done?

1793
01:58:52.292 --> 01:58:53.335
I'm tired, Dad.

1794
01:58:53.627 --> 01:58:54.669
Forgive me.

1795
01:58:55.587 --> 01:58:57.297
I can't fight anymore.

1796
01:58:59.174 --> 01:59:01.926
"Such anger..."

1797
01:59:03.345 --> 01:59:06.598
"Let me tell you a secret"

1798
01:59:07.474 --> 01:59:11.852
"This body is an empty shell"

1799
01:59:11.853 --> 01:59:15.065
"lts spirit...
its soul... is you."

1800
01:59:19.986 --> 01:59:21.070
So as I was saying...

1801
01:59:21.071 --> 01:59:23.572
She's an optimist,
she has her dreams...

1802
01:59:23.573 --> 01:59:26.117
but she's not afraid
to write her own life story.

1803
01:59:28.536 --> 01:59:32.791
"Without you, my love,"

1804
01:59:33.083 --> 01:59:37.796
"My heart is
a deserted island"

1805
01:59:40.048 --> 01:59:41.091
Why are you here, Krish?

1806
01:59:42.384 --> 01:59:43.385
To say sorry.

1807
01:59:44.302 --> 01:59:45.470
It's not your fault.

1808
01:59:47.430 --> 01:59:49.224
But I'm the one suffering.

1809
01:59:51.267 --> 01:59:52.769
You look terrible...

1810
01:59:59.484 --> 02:00:03.279
You know your mom will
never accept my family.

1811
02:00:06.116 --> 02:00:07.283
Let's run away?

1812
02:00:14.749 --> 02:00:17.626
Isn't it enough that
we love each other?

1813
02:00:17.627 --> 02:00:18.878
It's never enough...

1814
02:00:19.337 --> 02:00:21.464
Ananya, you're killing me.

1815
02:00:22.757 --> 02:00:25.134
You think it's
not hard for me?

1816
02:00:25.135 --> 02:00:27.887
If it's hard,
then why are you doing this?

1817
02:00:29.472 --> 02:00:32.225
So that we both stop
hurting each other.

1818
02:00:33.601 --> 02:00:35.395
I love you, Ananya.

1819
02:00:38.481 --> 02:00:39.941
Please leave, Krish.

1820
02:00:46.614 --> 02:00:47.657
Listen.

1821
02:00:50.702 --> 02:00:52.662
Please, stop calling me.

1822
02:00:54.789 --> 02:00:55.874
Otherwise...

1823
02:00:58.001 --> 02:01:00.754
Otherwise, I'll have
to block your number.

1824
02:01:08.219 --> 02:01:11.473
"Without you... there's
no fire in the sun"

1825
02:01:12.474 --> 02:01:15.518
"No song in the songbird"

1826
02:01:16.352 --> 02:01:20.774
"if the moon reigns
with such abandon"

1827
02:01:21.024 --> 02:01:24.735
"Why is there only
darkness in my grasp?"

1828
02:01:24.736 --> 02:01:28.740
"These incomplete stories..."

1829
02:01:29.324 --> 02:01:32.202
"And incomplete goodbyes"

1830
02:01:33.161 --> 02:01:37.248
"Will they remain
incomplete..."

1831
02:01:37.707 --> 02:01:40.919
"... forever?"

1832
02:01:41.377 --> 02:01:46.256
"These incomplete stories..."

1833
02:01:46.257 --> 02:01:49.511
"And incomplete goodbyes"

1834
02:01:50.053 --> 02:01:54.765
"Will they remain
incomplete..."

1835
02:01:54.766 --> 02:01:57.811
"... forever?"

1836
02:01:59.604 --> 02:02:03.900
"Without you, my love,"

1837
02:02:04.275 --> 02:02:10.323
"The days feel like rivers,
islanded by the nights..."

1838
02:02:15.578 --> 02:02:16.830
I need some help.

1839
02:02:18.790 --> 02:02:19.833
I..-

1840
02:02:20.583 --> 02:02:22.126
I want to kill myself.

1841
02:02:24.671 --> 02:02:25.713
Suicide.

1842
02:02:28.007 --> 02:02:31.469
Actually, I had come
to you for sleeping pills...

1843
02:02:34.722 --> 02:02:38.017
My folks don't believe
in counselling.

1844
02:02:39.644 --> 02:02:44.232
Punjabis thinks only crazy
people go to psychiatrists.

1845
02:03:26.232 --> 02:03:28.026
You came home pretty
late last night...

1846
02:03:29.402 --> 02:03:30.486
ls everything okay?

1847
02:03:41.289 --> 02:03:44.626
My pension papers are held up.

1848
02:03:45.835 --> 02:03:49.672
I need a letter typed...

1849
02:03:49.881 --> 02:03:52.175
On the laptop...

1850
02:03:52.592 --> 02:03:53.635
I'll do it.

1851
02:03:57.013 --> 02:03:58.139
Thank you.

1852
02:04:07.941 --> 02:04:09.359
How's your friend?

1853
02:04:10.818 --> 02:04:11.945
Which friend?

1854
02:04:13.363 --> 02:04:14.822
The one from Chennai...

1855
02:04:15.365 --> 02:04:16.783
who was at Minty's wedding.

1856
02:04:18.534 --> 02:04:20.119
I don't know.
She's probably fine.

1857
02:04:22.455 --> 02:04:23.456
Why don't you know?

1858
02:04:24.999 --> 02:04:26.250
Aren't you'll in touch?

1859
02:04:28.670 --> 02:04:30.546
Everyone's busy
with their own lives.

1860
02:04:40.515 --> 02:04:41.557
I'm going to bed.

1861
02:04:44.227 --> 02:04:48.564
If we try... we can...
speak to one another...

1862
02:04:53.903 --> 02:04:54.904
Good night.

1863
02:04:55.238 --> 02:04:57.532
I'll give you the
printout tomorrow.

1864
02:05:18.636 --> 02:05:19.679
Where's Dad?

1865
02:05:21.472 --> 02:05:23.599
Do me a favour
and shave at least?

1866
02:05:24.183 --> 02:05:26.060
I want you to meet a girl.

1867
02:05:26.686 --> 02:05:28.146
If the money's good,
just say yes.

1868
02:05:31.357 --> 02:05:34.444
Look, Krish. I've never
forced you to do anything.

1869
02:05:34.986 --> 02:05:36.987
Don't behave
like this with me.

1870
02:05:36.988 --> 02:05:38.197
Then how should I behave?

1871
02:05:38.948 --> 02:05:40.032
Fine.

1872
02:05:40.033 --> 02:05:41.909
I'll just shut up, then.

1873
02:05:42.869 --> 02:05:45.705
First my husband, now my son.

1874
02:05:46.497 --> 02:05:51.335
I thought at least my in-laws would
respect me once you got married...

1875
02:05:51.836 --> 02:05:53.796
but no.

1876
02:05:54.255 --> 02:05:56.966
You want me to go and
beg in front of those Madrasis.

1877
02:05:58.259 --> 02:06:01.470
Shipra's right.
Everyone is selfish. Everyone.

1878
02:06:01.471 --> 02:06:03.139
I've never, ever refused you.

1879
02:06:04.140 --> 02:06:07.393
I'm tired of making
up for Dad's faults.

1880
02:06:09.520 --> 02:06:10.938
That's why I'm in this state.

1881
02:06:15.359 --> 02:06:16.778
What are you trying to say?

1882
02:06:17.945 --> 02:06:21.115
For once in life, I needed your help.
And what did you do? You turned away.

1883
02:06:21.741 --> 02:06:22.867
Where do I go now?

1884
02:06:24.410 --> 02:06:25.578
I'm a fool.

1885
02:06:27.330 --> 02:06:28.790
I disgust myself!

1886
02:06:30.333 --> 02:06:34.545
I love Ananya and
I'm still letting her go.

1887
02:06:44.180 --> 02:06:47.767
Mom, you talk of community,
religion, Madrasis, Punjabis...

1888
02:06:49.435 --> 02:06:52.647
you married a Punjabi,
right? What came of it?

1889
02:08:17.231 --> 02:08:18.232
And where were you?

1890
02:08:20.067 --> 02:08:21.194
What is it to you?

1891
02:08:23.279 --> 02:08:25.323
This family is beyond repair.

1892
02:08:51.140 --> 02:08:52.141
Hello?

1893
02:08:53.226 --> 02:08:54.268
Hello?

1894
02:08:56.604 --> 02:08:57.563
Krish.

1895
02:09:00.107 --> 02:09:01.150
Ananya...

1896
02:09:03.611 --> 02:09:05.154
Did you mis-dial?

1897
02:09:06.030 --> 02:09:07.490
I'm sorry about
the other day...

1898
02:09:08.824 --> 02:09:10.451
But you could have told me.

1899
02:09:11.702 --> 02:09:12.869
What?

1900
02:09:12.870 --> 02:09:14.997
That your dad was
coming to my house.

1901
02:09:18.084 --> 02:09:19.210
What do you mean?

1902
02:09:19.919 --> 02:09:23.381
He spent the whole
day with Mom and Dad...

1903
02:09:24.590 --> 02:09:26.676
He apologized on
behalf of your mother.

1904
02:09:27.718 --> 02:09:29.845
MY dad... apologized?

1905
02:09:30.346 --> 02:09:31.472
Yes.

1906
02:09:32.181 --> 02:09:33.849
My parents are so happy!

1907
02:09:34.267 --> 02:09:38.896
In fact, they asked if
we had a date in mind.

1908
02:09:44.026 --> 02:09:45.152
Is there?

1909
02:09:48.990 --> 02:09:50.825
A date you have in mind?

1910
02:09:52.827 --> 02:09:54.036
Krish...

1911
02:09:54.412 --> 02:09:57.123
In trying to bring
everyone together...

1912
02:09:58.499 --> 02:09:59.959
have we grown apart?

1913
02:10:01.127 --> 02:10:02.545
I haven't gone away, Ananya.

1914
02:10:02.920 --> 02:10:04.171
I'm right here.

1915
02:10:06.048 --> 02:10:07.300
I love you, Krish.

1916
02:10:09.969 --> 02:10:11.220
Me too, Ananya.

1917
02:10:12.638 --> 02:10:14.223
Do you mean it?

1918
02:10:15.850 --> 02:10:17.184
I'm losing my mind...

1919
02:10:18.144 --> 02:10:19.895
I can't eat or sleep.

1920
02:10:20.855 --> 02:10:23.065
All I think about is you.

1921
02:10:23.983 --> 02:10:25.234
Isn't it clear?

1922
02:10:25.818 --> 02:10:27.111
I love you.

1923
02:10:31.032 --> 02:10:32.033
Good.

1924
02:10:34.076 --> 02:10:35.411
Now, it seems convincing.

1925
02:10:39.832 --> 02:10:41.042
Hang on.

1926
02:10:41.459 --> 02:10:43.878
My dad was at your house?

1927
02:10:44.754 --> 02:10:46.005
Didn't you know?

1928
02:10:46.839 --> 02:10:47.882
No...

1929
02:10:49.467 --> 02:10:50.885
We'll talk in the morning.

1930
02:10:51.177 --> 02:10:52.345
Yes...

1931
02:10:53.679 --> 02:10:54.680
Good night.

1932
02:10:54.930 --> 02:10:56.057
Good night.

1933
02:12:17.721 --> 02:12:19.014
Did you go to Chennai?

1934
02:12:24.228 --> 02:12:25.354
Thank you.

1935
02:12:30.151 --> 02:12:31.360
You knew.

1936
02:12:34.572 --> 02:12:37.283
I'm a bad man.
Not a stupid one.

1937
02:12:39.660 --> 02:12:43.330
I didn't want to lose
my son in my old age.

1938
02:12:46.167 --> 02:12:47.334
They're nice...

1939
02:12:48.377 --> 02:12:50.671
Ananya's parents,
nice people.

1940
02:12:51.172 --> 02:12:52.256
Yes...

1941
02:12:57.595 --> 02:13:01.432
I can't come to
your wedding, Krish.

1942
02:13:07.104 --> 02:13:09.273
For the first time in years
I've done something right...

1943
02:13:10.900 --> 02:13:12.860
I'm afraid...
if I come... I'll ruin it...

1944
02:13:15.279 --> 02:13:19.074
You know I can't get along
with your mother's family.

1945
02:13:19.658 --> 02:13:21.160
You won't come to my wedding?

1946
02:13:22.828 --> 02:13:25.122
Look, Ananya is
coming to our home.

1947
02:13:26.040 --> 02:13:27.166
Right?

1948
02:13:27.625 --> 02:13:30.419
Then why do you want
to put me through my paces?

1949
02:13:40.804 --> 02:13:41.846
That day...

1950
02:13:41.847 --> 02:13:43.557
I wanted to hug my father.

1951
02:13:46.602 --> 02:13:48.521
But that would've
been melodramatic, right?

1952
02:13:50.981 --> 02:13:53.234
Suddenly if everything
falls into place...

1953
02:13:54.276 --> 02:13:55.778
life becomes boring.

1954
02:13:58.197 --> 02:13:59.532
Okay, tell me what happens
in a Brahmin wedding.

1955
02:13:59.949 --> 02:14:00.991
A lot.

1956
02:14:01.242 --> 02:14:03.202
Prepare your family
to see a lot of new rituals.

1957
02:14:03.577 --> 02:14:05.538
All Punjabis want
to see is alcohol.

1958
02:14:06.997 --> 02:14:08.082
Done!

1959
02:14:10.417 --> 02:14:11.961
Everything will be fine, right?

1960
02:14:13.546 --> 02:14:14.587
Of course.

1961
02:14:14.588 --> 02:14:16.006
Ananya, come here.

1962
02:14:17.007 --> 02:14:18.676
Come soon.
I miss you.

1963
02:14:18.968 --> 02:14:20.177
I miss you, too.

1964
02:14:48.581 --> 02:14:50.040
"H "

1965
02:14:51.709 --> 02:14:53.210
"H "

1966
02:14:54.795 --> 02:14:57.672
"The bride and groom
make a gorgeous pair!"

1967
02:14:57.673 --> 02:15:01.260
Just pray we don't get
fall sick with all that sambar!

1968
02:15:03.095 --> 02:15:04.305
Joke!

1969
02:15:04.638 --> 02:15:07.141
"Breaking traditions
and reigning chaos"

1970
02:15:07.725 --> 02:15:13.689
"Weaving a love story
on the crossroads of destiny"

1971
02:15:13.897 --> 02:15:17.025
"The pongal pot is boiling
My love speaks to you"

1972
02:15:17.026 --> 02:15:20.069
"The husband brings
good luck, girl"

1973
02:15:20.070 --> 02:15:23.114
"Running with love
Did she catch me?"

1974
02:15:23.115 --> 02:15:25.826
"Or was she caught?"

1975
02:15:25.993 --> 02:15:29.078
"Here comes the
bride's carriage"

1976
02:15:29.079 --> 02:15:32.248
"With the fancy band dancing"

1977
02:15:32.249 --> 02:15:37.046
"Symphonising with trumpets!"

1978
02:15:37.379 --> 02:15:38.756
Namaste.

1979
02:15:41.550 --> 02:15:42.800
Excuse me...

1980
02:15:42.801 --> 02:15:44.928
Can we have a word with you?

1981
02:15:46.847 --> 02:15:47.806
Of course.

1982
02:15:50.267 --> 02:15:53.269
"Hope springs in the air"

1983
02:15:53.270 --> 02:15:54.313
"H "

1984
02:15:56.440 --> 02:15:57.691
"Oh, the bride..."

1985
02:15:59.485 --> 02:16:00.819
"H "

1986
02:16:03.322 --> 02:16:04.490
What happened?

1987
02:16:05.866 --> 02:16:07.910
They asked us what
gifts we wanted!

1988
02:16:08.160 --> 02:16:09.370
What did you ask for?

1989
02:16:09.662 --> 02:16:12.915
TV? Fridge? Bungalow? Boat!

1990
02:16:13.165 --> 02:16:14.457
Do I think I'm crazy?

1991
02:16:14.458 --> 02:16:17.794
She didn't ask for anything!
She got emotional unnecessarily!

1992
02:16:17.795 --> 02:16:20.421
She said she wished for
one MBA, she'd getting two!

1993
02:16:20.422 --> 02:16:22.383
What better gift than that?!

1994
02:16:22.675 --> 02:16:24.301
<i>'</i> Really?
<i>'</i> Yes!

1995
02:16:24.760 --> 02:16:26.595
You know what your
problem is, Krish?

1996
02:16:27.262 --> 02:16:29.556
You have no idea
how much I love you.

1997
02:16:30.933 --> 02:16:32.184
Let's

1998
02:16:37.022 --> 02:16:39.525
Who on earth gets married
at 6.30 in the morning?!

1999
02:16:40.067 --> 02:16:42.194
Only yoga classes
happen that early!

2000
02:16:42.986 --> 02:16:44.196
Boy's father?

2001
02:16:46.782 --> 02:16:47.866
Just a second!

2002
02:16:52.705 --> 02:16:54.957
- Coffee?
- Yes, please.

2003
02:17:56.810 --> 02:18:00.689
"I can't tear my eyes away"

2004
02:18:02.691 --> 02:18:07.279
"As they seek your
acceptance, too"

2005
02:18:08.489 --> 02:18:13.786
"The kohl of your eyes
tinges my days"

2006
02:18:14.244 --> 02:18:19.244
"While the smell of your
perfume haunts my nights"

2007
02:18:19.291 --> 02:18:22.043
"Spellbound, this mind..."

2008
02:18:22.044 --> 02:18:24.755
"Speaks only your name"

2009
02:18:25.047 --> 02:18:27.965
"Spellbound, this mind..."

2010
02:18:27.966 --> 02:18:30.511
"Speaks only your name"

2011
02:18:31.220 --> 02:18:34.555
"Would that it could... "

2012
02:18:34.556 --> 02:18:36.682
but it can't forget"

2013
02:18:36.683 --> 02:18:39.560
"Spellbound, this mind..."

2014
02:18:39.561 --> 02:18:42.396
"Speaks only your name"

2015
02:18:42.397 --> 02:18:45.316
"Spellbound, this mind..."

2016
02:18:45.317 --> 02:18:49.863
"Speaks only your name"

2017
02:18:51.949 --> 02:18:55.368
The boy's mother will sit there...

2018
02:18:55.369 --> 02:18:58.996
and if the father isn't here,
then any senior member can-

2019
02:18:58.997 --> 02:19:00.040
Father is here.

2020
02:19:21.687 --> 02:19:22.855
What is he doing here?

2021
02:19:24.523 --> 02:19:25.774
He arrived last night.

2022
02:19:27.901 --> 02:19:29.069
Namaste!

2023
02:19:29.611 --> 02:19:30.779
Please.

2024
02:20:17.618 --> 02:20:19.286
I've made a lot of mistakes...

2025
02:20:24.750 --> 02:20:27.044
will you hate
me all my life?

2026
02:20:49.942 --> 02:20:54.942
"Our hearts sing the song
That tells our story"

2027
02:20:55.906 --> 02:20:57.824
Why do our parents
oppose this?

2028
02:20:59.242 --> 02:21:01.244
- It's not about communities...

2029
02:21:02.204 --> 02:21:06.083
It's about us finding love
without their consent...

2030
02:21:12.839 --> 02:21:17.469
If we fall in love with someone, doesn't
mean we love our parents any less...

2031
02:21:18.053 --> 02:21:20.639
Love doesn't need to be divided;
It's all encompassing.

2032
02:21:21.223 --> 02:21:25.686
They should be proud that, like them,
now our love is unconditional.

2033
02:21:41.576 --> 02:21:44.538
From our first word
to our first cigarette...

2034
02:21:44.997 --> 02:21:46.331
they've seen it all.

2035
02:21:47.207 --> 02:21:50.794
Now they suddenly
feel betrayed.

2036
02:21:51.378 --> 02:21:52.838
That's why they get angry.

2037
02:22:20.365 --> 02:22:24.327
Maybe after 25 years,
when we're in their shoes...

2038
02:22:24.786 --> 02:22:27.956
maybe then
we'll understand.
